<p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br /></p>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">⤱Critique⤱</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Nationalist&nbsp;Cheese</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<div style="text-align: left;">
<p>So first off, it feels weird that the GOC would send a team comprising of agents from the country involved in the conflict? I could think of some reasons such as familiarity with the surroundings, easier to blend in, quickest team to respond&lt; but I want to know what's your reason.</p>
<p>Now, I'm an Indian person (albeit not living in India) and so there's always been this rivalry between our two countries, not just from this issue. So I'm curious to see how you handle the tension between members of the two nationalities. Keep in mind however, to avoid any sort of bias in your storytelling. Remember, this is an ongoing political incident.</p>
<p>Besides that, the same will be said about the entire political incident. While you may have your opinions about who is write or wrong, <strong>DO NOT</strong> integrate them into your story. Make it as a neutral as it can be, so that you don't offend anyone. This is meant to be an article that can be read and understood by everyone.</p>
<p>Also, just a minor detail, is the team being sent in Assessment or STRIKE? These teams have 2 different purposes as well as operating procedures, so make your choices and integrate it into the story.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
<span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span>
<hr />
<p><span style="white-space: pre-wrap;">&#32;</span><br />
<strong>Conclusion:</strong> Overall, you have an interesting storyline here, that is worth pursuing. However, do be careful of how you portray the conflict, since it is a sensitive issue.</p>
<p>Once you have made the adjustments, or you have any questions, feel free to reach out to me on Wikidot PM or on IRC chat.</p>

