<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Page Type: Other (GOC Entry)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>To be real clear here: you mean you're wanting to write a GOC goi-format in the style of e.g. <a href="/kte-5634-ex-machina-bosch">KTE-5634-Ex-Machina-Bosch</a>?</p>
<hr />
<p>My, big concern with this pitch is that I have a good idea of you wanting to like, get into the conflict between the GOC members as an analogue for like border disputes, and to really explore how this infighting affects them; but my concern is that you've spent a lot of time talking in the generic and I don't really know if you've nailed down the specific: that is, how this conflict between members is actually intended to play out. Like, how does it escalate? How does it end up getting resolved? What does happen when a team composed of these two nations that hate each other are sent on a mission in the background of their heated political dispute?</p>
<p>I have some concerns about this as a GoI Format: it feels to me that a tale would allow you to write this conflict a lot more effectively, with less of a worry about how you include this lengthy conflict in a way that feels like&#8230;appropriately cold and clinical? Like, the threat entity database entry idea is great when the GOC are unified and when you can tell a story in a very detached and cold way; but it feels to me that this wants to really get into the story and really intimately play with the characters?</p>
</div>
</div>
