<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>But I can't really dedicate myself to figuring out how to write this draft into this format without the green lights for the concept first. That's what the Drafts and Critiques forum is for, right?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Uhhh sort of but not really; the drafts critique forum is for giving feedback on this as a draft and assumes you have attempted to answer the question of 'how do you get this into the format' already. Whereas I want to know you've at least considered it because guess what buddy: the format imposes restrictions on how you can tell the story; and if you don't consider how those restrictions are gonna impact the story telling, you're gonna have a bad day when you try to write this.</p>
<hr />
<p>As for the actual longer form exploration, I'm kinda&#8230;torn on it. If executed well, this could be really good, and I can totally see this working well; but it feels like is has a lot of potential to be really dry and boring, and I think what'll really elevate this is the characterisation: making everyone really feel real, and showing enough of the monster that it feels like a viable threat; and like&#8230;really having us understand why what's happening is interesting.</p>
<p>I'm still really not convinced by this as a goi-format: it really feels like a lot of this detail would be best kept as a tale; since like, it feels like a lot of times this would be quiet informal stuff you don't necessarily want to admit to doing in an official report (e.g., the two indian soldiers being ordered to shoot the chinese ones if they return alone).</p>
<p>I will <span style="color: green">greenlight</span> this under the assumption you deeply think about how you tell this story and really consider what the best format for it is.</p>
</div>
